From: Zhymabek Roman <zhymabekroman@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: Treat VREFRESH of 1 as 60 Hz compositor rate.

The X11 driver reports GetDeviceCaps(VREFRESH) == 1 under headless
displays (Xvfb) and some virtualized GPUs. The composite thread computed
refresh_period = 1000 / 1 = 1000 ms, throttling the DirectComposition
presenter to 1 frame per second. Guard the documented non-value:
treat frequency <= 1 as the 60 Hz default.

Signed-off-by: Zhymabek Roman <zhymabekroman@gmail.com>
---
 dlls/dcomp/device.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/dcomp/device.c b/dlls/dcomp/device.c
index 1ea3728a1..f0c9d3e2b 100644
--- a/dlls/dcomp/device.c
+++ b/dlls/dcomp/device.c
@@ -1060,7 +1060,7 @@ static DWORD WINAPI composite_thread_proc( void *param )
     /* TODO: Implement and use D3DKMTWaitForVerticalBlankEvent() */
     hdc = GetDC(0);
     frequency = hdc ? GetDeviceCaps(hdc, VREFRESH) : 0;
-    if (frequency <= 0) frequency = 60;
+    if (frequency <= 1) frequency = 60;
     refresh_period = 1000 / frequency;
     if (refresh_period == 0) refresh_period = 16;
     if (hdc) ReleaseDC(0, hdc);
--
2.48.1
